1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,008
What's today's video about? It's about Japanese festivals!

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:13,008
Scene 1: The Charm of the Nebuta Festival

3
00:00:13,008 --> 00:00:17,391
Where are you going for summer vacation this year?

4
00:00:17,414 --> 00:00:19,830
I'm going to Aomori.

5
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:22,870
I'm going to see the Nebuta Festival!

6
00:00:22,893 --> 00:00:25,411
The Nebuta Festival?

7
00:00:25,434 --> 00:00:28,051
What kind of festival is it?

8
00:00:28,074 --> 00:00:32,457
Huge floats parade through the streets.

9
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:35,930
Are the floats made of wood?

10
00:00:35,953 --> 00:00:39,437
No, they're made of paper.

11
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:43,076
There are lots of lights inside them.

12
00:00:43,099 --> 00:00:46,549
They must be beautiful at night!

13
00:00:46,572 --> 00:00:53,022
Yes, the glowing floats light up the night—it's stunning!

14
00:00:53,045 --> 00:00:55,869
Do you just watch the floats?

15
00:00:55,892 --> 00:00:59,580
No, everyone dances together too!

16
00:00:59,604 --> 00:01:03,020
Are the dance steps hard?

17
00:01:03,043 --> 00:01:06,027
No, they're easy!

18
00:01:06,051 --> 00:01:08,191
We jump and dance!

19
00:01:08,214 --> 00:01:10,400
That sounds like fun!

20
00:01:10,423 --> 00:01:12,840
I want to go too!

21
00:01:12,863 --> 00:01:16,046
Then let's go together!

22
00:01:16,069 --> 00:01:20,352
Is Aomori far from Tokyo?

23
00:01:20,375 --> 00:01:24,625
It takes about three hours by Shinkansen.

24
00:01:24,648 --> 00:01:27,338
Did you already buy your tickets?

25
00:01:27,361 --> 00:01:30,217
Yes, I bought them yesterday.

26
00:01:30,241 --> 00:01:32,457
That's great!

27
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:35,808
Make sure to take lots of photos of the festival!

28
00:01:35,832 --> 00:01:38,482
And I'll bring back some souvenirs too!

29
00:01:38,505 --> 00:01:39,755
Thank you!

30
00:01:39,778 --> 00:01:42,161
Have a safe trip!

31
00:01:42,184 --> 00:01:49,289
You can review today's video with the link in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

32
00:01:49,289 --> 00:01:52,289
Scene 2: Introduction to Akita's Kanto Festival

33
00:01:52,289 --> 00:01:55,106
Take a look at this photo.

34
00:01:55,129 --> 00:01:59,819
Wow, there are so many lights!

35
00:01:59,842 --> 00:02:03,782
This is Akita's Kanto Festival.

36
00:02:03,805 --> 00:02:07,105
The Kanto Festival?

37
00:02:07,128 --> 00:02:09,145
What is it?

38
00:02:09,168 --> 00:02:14,185
They attach lots of lanterns to long bamboo poles.

39
00:02:14,208 --> 00:02:17,340
How many lanterns are there?

40
00:02:17,363 --> 00:02:20,213
Forty-six lanterns!

41
00:02:20,236 --> 00:02:22,653
That must be really heavy!

42
00:02:22,676 --> 00:02:25,492
What do they do with it?

43
00:02:25,515 --> 00:02:29,532
A single man carries it.

44
00:02:29,555 --> 00:02:31,538
With his hands?

45
00:02:31,561 --> 00:02:36,878
He holds it with his hands, then balances it on his shoulder or forehead.

46
00:02:36,901 --> 00:02:40,617
On his *forehead*?

47
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:43,090
Isn't that dangerous?

48
00:02:43,113 --> 00:02:47,381
They train a lot, so it's safe.

49
00:02:47,405 --> 00:02:50,288
That's an incredible skill!

50
00:02:50,311 --> 00:02:54,329
It must be really tough when the wind blows.

51
00:02:54,352 --> 00:02:56,474
Won't it fall over?

52
00:02:56,497 --> 00:03:01,193
They skillfully use their body to keep balance.

53
00:03:01,217 --> 00:03:05,000
It looks even more amazing up close!

54
00:03:05,023 --> 00:03:09,006
I want to go to Akita and see the real thing.

55
00:03:09,029 --> 00:03:11,613
It's in August, by the way.

56
00:03:11,636 --> 00:03:14,019
Want to go together?

57
00:03:14,042 --> 00:03:16,659
I'd love to!

58
00:03:16,682 --> 00:03:26,597
If you could catch that, leave a comment!

59
00:03:26,597 --> 00:03:29,597
Scene 3: Tanabata Festival Decorations

60
00:03:29,597 --> 00:03:36,290
There's a festival with decorations in August. Where is it held?

61
00:03:36,313 --> 00:03:39,649
It's the Sendai Tanabata Festival.

62
00:03:39,672 --> 00:03:42,189
The Tanabata Festival?

63
00:03:42,212 --> 00:03:44,742
What kind of decorations do they have?

64
00:03:44,765 --> 00:03:50,249
Long paper streamers line the streets everywhere.

65
00:03:50,272 --> 00:03:53,455
Are the decorations big?

66
00:03:53,478 --> 00:03:58,362
Yes, they're really big and long.

67
00:03:58,385 --> 00:04:01,201
How many meters long are they?

68
00:04:01,224 --> 00:04:04,568
About five meters long.

69
00:04:04,592 --> 00:04:07,342
Wow, that's tall!

70
00:04:07,365 --> 00:04:10,981
Don't they hit your head when you walk by?

71
00:04:11,004 --> 00:04:13,921
Yes, they do.

72
00:04:13,944 --> 00:04:18,194
You touch the decorations and walk underneath them.

73
00:04:18,217 --> 00:04:20,901
That sounds like fun!

74
00:04:20,924 --> 00:04:23,616
Do they come in different colors?

75
00:04:23,639 --> 00:04:29,167
Yes, there are many colors like red and blue—very colorful!

76
00:04:29,191 --> 00:04:32,051
Are they all made of paper?

77
00:04:32,074 --> 00:04:38,564
Yes, they carefully make new decorations every year.

78
00:04:38,587 --> 00:04:40,931
It's such a beautiful festival.

79
00:04:40,954 --> 00:04:44,238
I want to take lots of photos!

80
00:04:44,261 --> 00:04:48,289
There are also lots of food stalls.

81
00:04:48,312 --> 00:04:51,846
You can try delicious food from Sendai too.

82
00:04:51,869 --> 00:04:56,919
Yes, beef tongue and zunda mochi are famous.

83
00:04:56,942 --> 00:05:02,398
Healing decorations and delicious food—it's perfect!

84
00:05:02,421 --> 00:05:07,405
Yes, let's definitely go this summer!

85
00:05:07,428 --> 00:05:10,428
Scene 4: The Excitement of Kanda Festival

86
00:05:10,428 --> 00:05:15,081
Are there any famous festivals in Tokyo?

87
00:05:15,104 --> 00:05:18,729
Yes, the Kanda Festival is very famous.

88
00:05:18,752 --> 00:05:21,935
When is the Kanda Festival held?

89
00:05:21,958 --> 00:05:24,342
It's in May.

90
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:26,105
In May?

91
00:05:26,128 --> 00:05:28,548
That's not summer, is it?

92
00:05:28,571 --> 00:05:33,154
No, but it's a very lively festival.

93
00:05:33,177 --> 00:05:35,261
What do people do there?

94
00:05:35,284 --> 00:05:38,934
Many people carry mikoshi (portable shrines).

95
00:05:38,957 --> 00:05:42,140
How many mikoshi are there?

96
00:05:42,163 --> 00:05:44,659
Around 200.

97
00:05:44,682 --> 00:05:48,799
The streets get packed with people.

98
00:05:48,822 --> 00:05:50,739
200 mikoshi?

99
00:05:50,762 --> 00:05:53,510
That's incredible!

100
00:05:53,533 --> 00:05:59,069
Yes, everyone shouts loudly and walks energetically.

101
00:05:59,092 --> 00:06:02,275
Will we walk around near Akihabara too?

102
00:06:02,298 --> 00:06:08,548
Yes, it's fascinating to see the portable shrine parade through the electric town.

103
00:06:08,571 --> 00:06:13,479
A perfect blend of a modern city and a traditional festival, isn't it?

104
00:06:13,503 --> 00:06:15,565
Exactly.

105
00:06:15,588 --> 00:06:19,642
You'll see lots of foreign tourists coming to watch too.

106
00:06:19,665 --> 00:06:23,382
I'd love to experience that atmosphere.

107
00:06:23,405 --> 00:06:27,293
There's a big festival every two years.

108
00:06:27,316 --> 00:06:29,374
When's the next one?

109
00:06:29,397 --> 00:06:31,449
Next year.

110
00:06:31,472 --> 00:06:33,589
Let's go together!

111
00:06:33,612 --> 00:06:35,960
I'm really looking forward to it.

112
00:06:35,983 --> 00:06:38,983
Scene 5: Gion Festival and the Magnificent Yamaboko Floats

113
00:06:38,983 --> 00:06:43,567
Have you heard of Kyoto's Gion Festival?

114
00:06:43,590 --> 00:06:46,806
I've heard the name before.

115
00:06:46,829 --> 00:06:49,485
It's a famous festival, right?

116
00:06:49,508 --> 00:06:53,625
Yes, it has over a thousand years of history.

117
00:06:53,648 --> 00:06:56,370
A thousand years?

118
00:06:56,393 --> 00:06:59,143
That's incredibly old.

119
00:06:59,166 --> 00:07:04,416
Throughout July, there are various events held.

120
00:07:04,439 --> 00:07:07,291
A whole month?

121
00:07:07,315 --> 00:07:09,857
That's surprisingly long.

122
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:15,610
The most famous part is the Yamaboko procession.

123
00:07:15,633 --> 00:07:18,151
What are Yamaboko?

124
00:07:18,174 --> 00:07:21,702
They're large floats made of wood.

125
00:07:21,726 --> 00:07:24,342
They're as tall as houses!

126
00:07:24,365 --> 00:07:28,627
How do they move those floats?

127
00:07:28,650 --> 00:07:34,267
A group of men pull them using long ropes.

128
00:07:34,290 --> 00:07:37,307
Is it hard to steer them?

129
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:42,792
Yes, turning at intersections takes a lot of time.

130
00:07:42,815 --> 00:07:44,865
Why is that?

131
00:07:44,888 --> 00:07:49,818
They lay bamboo under the wheels and pour water on it.

132
00:07:49,841 --> 00:07:52,691
Then they slide and turn the float.

133
00:07:52,714 --> 00:07:55,997
That sounds like quite a task.

134
00:07:56,020 --> 00:08:01,004
Yes, everyone works together to turn them slowly.

135
00:08:01,027 --> 00:08:03,643
That's one of the highlights.

136
00:08:03,666 --> 00:08:06,650
Are there nighttime events too?

137
00:08:06,673 --> 00:08:13,523
Yes, the night before the festival, lanterns light up the streets—it's beautiful.

138
00:08:13,546 --> 00:08:16,829
That must fit perfectly with Kyoto's historic streets.

139
00:08:16,852 --> 00:08:21,678
It's truly romantic and spectacular.

140
00:08:21,701 --> 00:08:24,701
Scene 6: The Charm of Tenjin Festival: Osaka's Summer River Celebration

141
00:08:24,701 --> 00:08:30,485
Have you ever been to Osaka's Tenjin Festival?

142
00:08:30,508 --> 00:08:32,428
No, I haven't.

143
00:08:32,451 --> 00:08:34,841
What kind of festival is it?

144
00:08:34,864 --> 00:08:40,447
It's the summer festival of Osaka, the 'City of Water'.

145
00:08:40,470 --> 00:08:43,487
The river becomes the stage.

146
00:08:43,510 --> 00:08:47,560
A river? That's unusual.

147
00:08:47,583 --> 00:08:54,875
Yes, over a hundred boats gather on the river starting in the evening.

148
00:08:54,898 --> 00:08:58,081
Over a hundred boats?

149
00:08:58,104 --> 00:09:01,588
What do they do on the boats?

150
00:09:01,611 --> 00:09:06,627
They play drums and dance energetically together.

151
00:09:06,650 --> 00:09:08,934
That sounds like fun!

152
00:09:08,958 --> 00:09:11,624
Can you see it near the river?

153
00:09:11,647 --> 00:09:16,933
Yes, you can view it from the bridge or along the riverside.

154
00:09:16,956 --> 00:09:20,240
Won't it be too dark at night?

155
00:09:20,263 --> 00:09:21,981
Don't worry.

156
00:09:22,005 --> 00:09:27,421
The boats are lit up with countless lights—it’s so bright!

157
00:09:27,444 --> 00:09:32,028
The reflections of the lights on the water must be beautiful, right?

158
00:09:32,050 --> 00:09:38,150
Yes, and the sky is filled with fireworks too!

159
00:09:38,174 --> 00:09:43,024
So you get to see both the fireworks and the boat lights together?

160
00:09:43,047 --> 00:09:44,763
Exactly.

161
00:09:44,786 --> 00:09:48,803
Osaka becomes so vibrant and lively!

162
00:09:48,826 --> 00:09:52,243
Do a lot of people come?

163
00:09:52,266 --> 00:09:58,449
Yes, over a million people attend every year.

164
00:09:58,472 --> 00:10:03,522
A million? That’s so popular!

165
00:10:03,545 --> 00:10:09,728
Absolutely! There are tons of food stalls with delicious treats too.

166
00:10:09,751 --> 00:10:14,401
I’d love to watch the festival while eating takoyaki.

167
00:10:14,424 --> 00:10:16,510
That sounds amazing!

168
00:10:16,533 --> 00:10:18,950
Let’s go together next time!

169
00:10:18,973 --> 00:10:21,973
Scene 7: The Thrill of the Kishiwada Danjiri Festival

170
00:10:21,973 --> 00:10:27,023
Osaka has another famous festival, you know.

171
00:10:27,046 --> 00:10:29,330
What’s it called?

172
00:10:29,353 --> 00:10:32,270
The Kishiwada Danjiri Festival.

173
00:10:32,293 --> 00:10:34,825
What’s a *danjiri*?

174
00:10:34,848 --> 00:10:38,231
It’s a large wooden float.

175
00:10:38,254 --> 00:10:40,838
Do people pull it?

176
00:10:40,861 --> 00:10:42,315
Yes.

177
00:10:42,338 --> 00:10:47,755
Around 500 people grab long ropes and run with all their might.

178
00:10:47,778 --> 00:10:49,961
They *run* with it?

179
00:10:49,984 --> 00:10:52,034
Isn't that dangerous?

180
00:10:52,057 --> 00:10:56,357
They take the corners at full speed—it’s so fast!

181
00:10:56,380 --> 00:11:01,597
Wait, they don’t slow down when turning? No, they don’t!

182
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:05,037
That’s the coolest part!

183
00:11:05,060 --> 00:11:08,243
Is someone riding on top?

184
00:11:08,266 --> 00:11:09,590
Yes.

185
00:11:09,613 --> 00:11:13,073
Yes, a man called the *daikugata* stands on it.

186
00:11:13,096 --> 00:11:15,780
What does he do up there?

187
00:11:15,803 --> 00:11:19,619
He jumps and dances on the moving float!

188
00:11:19,642 --> 00:11:22,774
On a *moving* float?!

189
00:11:22,798 --> 00:11:25,814
His balance is incredible!

190
00:11:25,837 --> 00:11:27,363
Yes.

191
00:11:27,387 --> 00:11:30,103
It’s so thrilling to watch!

192
00:11:30,126 --> 00:11:33,178
This festival is full of excitement!

193
00:11:33,201 --> 00:11:35,185
When does it take place?

194
00:11:35,208 --> 00:11:38,091
In September and October.

195
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:41,364
I’d love to see that powerful run!

196
00:11:41,387 --> 00:11:44,204
Let’s definitely go to Kishiwada!

197
00:11:44,227 --> 00:11:47,243
Just make sure to watch from a safe spot!

198
00:11:47,266 --> 00:11:50,266
Scene 8: Introduction to Awa Odori Dance

199
00:11:50,266 --> 00:11:54,350
Have you heard of Awa Odori in Tokushima?

200
00:11:54,373 --> 00:11:58,356
Yes, it’s a famous dance festival!

201
00:11:58,379 --> 00:12:02,462
It has over 400 years of history!

202
00:12:02,485 --> 00:12:06,971
400 years? That’s amazing!

203
00:12:06,994 --> 00:12:12,054
For four days in August, everyone dances in the streets!

204
00:12:12,078 --> 00:12:14,728
What kind of costumes do they wear?

205
00:12:14,751 --> 00:12:21,634
Men wear *happi* coats, and women wear *yukata* with straw hats.

206
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:27,165
The way they dance with those woven hats on looks so elegant.

207
00:12:27,188 --> 00:12:32,530
Yes, they wear geta sandals on their feet and dance by lifting them high.

208
00:12:32,553 --> 00:12:36,213
The clacking sound they make is so lively and fun.

209
00:12:36,237 --> 00:12:39,123
The music is really unique too.

210
00:12:39,146 --> 00:12:42,638
The sounds of the shamisen and taiko drums resonate through the air.

211
00:12:42,661 --> 00:12:47,478
Just listening to it makes you want to move your body!

212
00:12:47,501 --> 00:12:55,751
There's a famous song that goes, 'Fools who dance, fools who watch—if you're both fools, you might as well dance!'

213
00:12:55,774 --> 00:12:58,090
What does that mean?

214
00:12:58,113 --> 00:13:05,453
It means that since both the dancers and the spectators are in the same boat, you might as well join in and dance!

215
00:13:05,477 --> 00:13:07,997
That’s a fun song!

216
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:11,324
Can I join in and dance too?

217
00:13:11,347 --> 00:13:13,933
Of course, you can!

218
00:13:13,956 --> 00:13:17,173
There are places where anyone can participate.

219
00:13:17,196 --> 00:13:22,344
Alright, I’ll go all out and dance without holding back!

220
00:13:22,367 --> 00:13:23,823
Nice!

221
00:13:23,846 --> 00:13:27,502
Let’s all have fun and wear big smiles together.

222
00:13:27,526 --> 00:13:31,612
Looks like this summer is all about Tokushima!

223
00:13:31,635 --> 00:13:34,635
Scene 9: The Charm of Kochi’s Yosakoi Festival

224
00:13:34,635 --> 00:13:39,961
Have you ever heard of Kochi’s Yosakoi Festival?

225
00:13:39,984 --> 00:13:44,367
I’ve heard the name, but what kind of festival is it?

226
00:13:44,390 --> 00:13:49,874
It’s a bit like the Awa Odori, but much more modern.

227
00:13:49,897 --> 00:13:52,113
Modern?

228
00:13:52,136 --> 00:13:54,682
What’s the difference?

229
00:13:54,706 --> 00:13:57,756
The music is totally free—any genre goes!

230
00:13:57,779 --> 00:14:01,262
They even use rock and samba music!

231
00:14:01,285 --> 00:14:04,179
Rock music at a festival? That sounds so fresh and fun!

232
00:14:04,202 --> 00:14:08,222
It’s super innovative and exciting, right?

233
00:14:08,245 --> 00:14:15,031
Yes! Each team has completely different outfits and dance styles.

234
00:14:15,054 --> 00:14:17,704
The outfits are free too?

235
00:14:17,728 --> 00:14:23,311
Yep! They’re often colorful and really beautiful.

236
00:14:23,334 --> 00:14:27,618
Do they use any props when they dance?

237
00:14:27,641 --> 00:14:32,759
They carry naruko—wooden instruments.

238
00:14:32,782 --> 00:14:34,832
Naruko?

239
00:14:34,855 --> 00:14:37,719
What kind of sound do they make?

240
00:14:37,743 --> 00:14:42,249
They make a sharp *click-clack* sound to keep the rhythm.

241
00:14:42,272 --> 00:14:46,889
How many people are in one team?

242
00:14:46,912 --> 00:14:51,606
Some big teams have over 100 dancers!

243
00:14:51,629 --> 00:14:56,957
A hundred people dancing in sync—it must be so powerful!

244
00:14:56,980 --> 00:15:03,430
Yes! There are stages all over the city, and it stays lively until night.

245
00:15:03,453 --> 00:15:06,703
It must be really popular with young people.

246
00:15:06,726 --> 00:15:11,510
Absolutely—people come from all over the country!

247
00:15:11,532 --> 00:15:15,076
I’d love to see some intense dance battles!

248
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:20,516
It’s in August, so make sure to keep your schedule open!

249
00:15:20,539 --> 00:15:23,539
Scene 10: The Exciting Hakata Gion Yamakasa Festival

250
00:15:23,539 --> 00:15:28,401
Finally, let me introduce a festival from Fukuoka.

251
00:15:28,425 --> 00:15:31,708
You mean the Hakata Gion Yamakasa Festival, right?

252
00:15:31,731 --> 00:15:34,823
You know it well!

253
00:15:34,846 --> 00:15:39,729
This is a fiery festival for men.

254
00:15:39,752 --> 00:15:42,469
What do they do?

255
00:15:42,492 --> 00:15:47,948
They carry these incredibly heavy decorated floats called *yamakasa* and race through the streets.

256
00:15:47,971 --> 00:15:51,107
How much does it weigh?

257
00:15:51,131 --> 00:15:54,039
It weighs about a ton.

258
00:15:54,062 --> 00:15:56,588
A ton?

259
00:15:56,611 --> 00:15:59,894
You have to carry that and run?

260
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:01,167
Yes.

261
00:16:01,190 --> 00:16:06,440
There are several teams competing in a 5K race to see who finishes fastest.

262
00:16:06,463 --> 00:16:09,313
So it's a speed race?

263
00:16:09,336 --> 00:16:12,553
How far do you run?

264
00:16:12,576 --> 00:16:16,159
The course is about 5 kilometers long.

265
00:16:16,182 --> 00:16:22,032
Running 5K while carrying a one-ton decoration sounds really tough.

266
00:16:22,055 --> 00:16:23,383
Yes.

267
00:16:23,407 --> 00:16:29,553
That's why spectators splash lots of water on the runners.

268
00:16:29,576 --> 00:16:32,826
The crowd gets really hyped up too!

269
00:16:32,849 --> 00:16:39,232
It's called 'Ikioi-mizu'—everyone splashes water forcefully.

270
00:16:39,255 --> 00:16:41,709
Is it okay if our clothes get wet?

271
00:16:41,732 --> 00:16:43,316
Yes.

272
00:16:43,339 --> 00:16:47,671
Everyone gets completely soaked and runs with everything they've got!

273
00:16:47,694 --> 00:16:50,877
What time does the festival start?

274
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:57,317
The main race kicks off at 4:59 AM.

275
00:16:57,340 --> 00:16:59,590
4 AM in the morning?

276
00:16:59,613 --> 00:17:02,099
That's super early!

277
00:17:02,122 --> 00:17:03,708
Yes.

278
00:17:03,731 --> 00:17:09,819
But the whole town gathers, cheering loudly.

279
00:17:09,843 --> 00:17:13,126
That's an incredible energy boost first thing in the morning!

280
00:17:13,149 --> 00:17:16,675
I'll wake up early to watch it!